# SOLID Principles

Apply SOLID on every change. Prefer small, focused modules over god files.

## SRP — Single Responsibility
One module/class/function = one reason to change.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — UI + fetch + validation in one component
// ✅ GOOD — validateInput(), fetchCoach(), CoachCard
```

## OCP — Open/Closed
Extend via composition/props/hooks; avoid editing core logic for every variant.

## LSP — Liskov Substitution
Subtypes must honor the parent contract. Don’t weaken preconditions or throw unexpected errors.

## ISP — Interface Segregation
Prefer narrow types/props. Don’t force callers to depend on unused fields.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
type UserService = { create; update; delete; sendEmail; exportCsv };

// ✅ GOOD
type UserWriter = { create; update; delete };
type UserNotifier = { sendEmail };
```

## DIP — Dependency Inversion
Depend on abstractions (interfaces, injected deps), not concrete DB/HTTP clients in business logic.

## DRY & Structure
- Extract shared logic once; don’t copy-paste variants.
- Keep side effects at boundaries (API routes, Server Actions).
- Prefer pure functions for domain rules.
